skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
title Monorepo — UCD artifact decoding and XML event parser
start
if (Path ends exactly in .zip?) then (yes)
 :Read whole archive; find end-of-central-directory;
 :Require nonzero entry count; read first central-directory entry;
 :Validate local header and payload bounds;
 if (Stored or deflated method?) then (yes)
  :Copy or inflate whole selected entry; require size and CRC;
 else (unsupported)
  :Return read failure;
  stop
 endif
else (plain)
 :Read whole XML file; reject empty bytes;
endif
while (More bytes?) is (yes)
 :Skip text until next tag;
 if (Comment, processing instruction or CDATA?) then (yes)
  :Skip to terminator; reject missing terminator;
 else (element)
  :Read ASCII-style name and quoted attribute pairs;
  :Reject malformed lexical delimiters;
  :Invoke start/end callbacks; self-closing tag invokes both;
 endif
endwhile (done)
:Return parser success;
stop
footer
Source-reviewed orchestration. Nested semantics remain open; no runtime acceptance
claimed. Complete XML event parser and both archive readers reviewed. The archive reader
selects the first entry; despite its name it does not require exactly one entry or
validate the entry filename. Parsing avoids a full AST but retains whole
compressed/inflated buffers; it is not bounded streaming from disk. The event parser has
no nesting stack, root/repertoire completeness check, entity-reference decoding or
duplicate-attribute rejection. ValidateUcdXml uses no-op callbacks, so lexical success is
not full UAX42/XML/repertoire conformance. Native snapshot callbacks add property
interpretation separately.
end footer

@enduml
